{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>When brethren dwell together</b> — juxtaposed with \"you shall not muzzle,\" to teach you: a yevamah who falls before one afflicted with boils — they do not muzzle her." "<b>And he has no son</b> — ס\"ת אונן עם אל\"ף, meaning: he shall not act as an אונן (one mourning before burial), who would thresh indoors and winnow outdoors. Therefore Scripture juxtaposed to him his threshing." "<b>For a wife and a yevamah</b> — ויבמה בעל כרחה by gematria."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:39.599066309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}